# `eslint-config-next` is consumed through FlatCompat in eslint.config.mjs, and
# FlatCompat resolves plugin names relative to the PROJECT ROOT rather than
# relative to the config that names them. Under pnpm's strict layout the
# plugins live inside .pnpm/ and are invisible from the root, so ESLint dies
# with "couldn't find the plugin eslint-plugin-react-hooks" — which is also why
# `next build` prints an ESLint failure and the DAL-boundary test cannot load
# the real config.
#
# Hoisting the eslint packages into the root node_modules is the documented
# pnpm remedy. It is scoped to eslint deliberately: this is not `shamefully-hoist`,
# and nothing else gets a phantom dependency it did not declare.
public-hoist-pattern[]=*eslint*
